Lean.PrettyPrinter.Unexpander\">Lean.PrettyPrinter.Unexpander</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Prints a product that ends in `EStack⟨⟩` as `EStack⟨e₁, e₂, …⟩`.","docLink":"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.unexpandEStack","kind":"def","line":58,"name":"Std.WP.unexpandEStack","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/EStack.lean#L58-L66"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.unexpandEStackEnd\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">WP</span>.<span class=\"name\">unexpandEStackEnd</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.PrettyPrinter.Unexpander\">Lean.PrettyPrinter.Unexpander</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Prints `EStackEnd` as `EStack⟨⟩`.","docLink":"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.unexpandEStackEnd","kind":"def","line":54,"name":"Std.WP.unexpandEStackEnd","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/EStack.lean#L54-L56"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.«termEstack⟨_⟩»\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">WP</span>.<span class=\"name\">«termEstack⟨_⟩»</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">Lean.ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Exception postcondition stack **value**: `estack⟨e₁, e₂⟩` is `(e₁, e₂, ())`.","docLink":"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.«termEstack⟨_⟩»","kind":"def","line":43,"name":"Std.WP.«termEstack⟨_⟩»","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/EStack.lean#L43-L44"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.«termEStack⟨_⟩»\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">WP</span>.<span class=\"name\">«termEStack⟨_⟩»</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.ParserDescr\">Lean.ParserDescr</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Exception postcondition stack **type**: `EStack⟨ε₁ → l, ε₂ → l⟩` is `(ε₁ → l) × (ε₂ → l) × EStack⟨⟩`.","docLink":"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.«termEStack⟨_⟩»","kind":"def","line":41,"name":"Std.WP.«termEStack⟨_⟩»","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/EStack.lean#L41-L42"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.EStackEnd.mk\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">WP</span>.<span class=\"name\">EStackEnd</span>.<span class=\"name\">mk</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.EStackEnd\">EStack⟨</a><a href=\"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.EStackEnd\">⟩</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The value of the last stack component. It reduces to `()`. It is a named constant, so only a\nstack value prints as `estack⟨…⟩`.","docLink":"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.EStackEnd.mk","kind":"def","line":37,"name":"Std.WP.EStackEnd.mk","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/EStack.lean#L37-L39"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">abbrev</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.EStackEnd\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">WP</span>.<span class=\"name\">EStackEnd</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The last component of an exception postcondition stack. It reduces to `Unit`, so every\n`Unit` instance applies. It is a named constant, so only a stack prints as `EStack⟨…⟩`.","docLink":"./Std/WP/EStack.html#Std.WP.EStackEnd","kind":"def","line":33,"name":"Std.WP.EStackEnd","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Std/WP/EStack.lean#L33-L35"}}],"imports":["Std.WP.Assertion"],"instances":[],"name":"Std.WP.EStack"}